  "last_updated": "2026-08-23",
  "mod_id": "tfm2_champ_pos_lock",
  "name": "Champion Position Lock",
  "version": "0.5.7",
  "description": "Restrict champions so they can only be used in the positions you choose.\n\n* Settings -> Gameplay -> 'Position Lock' lets you pick the allowed champions per position.\n  (Leave a position empty and every champion may play there.)\n* AI teams too - the enemy team, coach delegation and background league matches all obey\n  the same rule: restricted champions are only evaluated for positions you allowed.\n* At the position assignment (swap) stage, EVERY match - yours and every background\n  league game - is arranged to match your settings. If a full arrangement is impossible,\n  it gets as close as it can.\n* Your own line-up is arranged automatically once the draft ends, and if you swap two\n  slots by hand your choice is kept. (Delegating to the head coach re-arranges it again.)\n* If the arrangement cannot satisfy your settings, the confirm button is disabled and\n  hovering it explains why.\n* During your draft, champions that would make a valid line-up impossible are greyed out\n  and cannot be clicked, exactly like fearless. The lock lifts automatically when nothing\n  legal is left to pick.\n* The settings window has a class filter (Fighter / Marksman / Mage / Support / Assassin)\n  and a champion name search, so you can find what you want in a large roster.\n  (Convenience only - it does not change the restriction itself.)\n* The list shows only champions currently available (unreleased ones are excluded).\n\nNotes\n* Settings are stored per save (inside the save file - you must save the game to keep them).\n* Works with the ban card count set to 'Auto': the same rule the game itself uses is applied.\n* If a position has fewer champions than the minimum (which depends on the ban card count),\n  that position is treated as unrestricted - this prevents the draft from locking up.\n* If a position can no longer be filled at all, you get that many free picks, and you may\n  spend them at any point in the draft order.\n* The mod's UI text follows the game language (Korean / English).\n* The champion list is sorted by the display name in the current game language, and the\n  search matches that name.\n\nWindows only."
}